  "language_probability": 1,
  "text": "A QR code is not just a random pile of squares. It is data written in black and white. Each tiny module stands for a binary 0 or 1. The big corner squares help your camera find the code and its rotation. A clear border called the quiet zone separates it from everything else. Your phone reads the modules in a set order and rebuilds the message. Extra The error correction data is stored inside the pattern. It lets the reader repair missing or damaged parts. So scratches can be forgiven but only up to a limit. The code carries a message, a reading guide and a backup plan.",
